WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.370
-The president went on Fox News
and lied to millions of people

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:05.972
about the coronavirus outbreak

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.775
as his administration bungles
its response to the crisis.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.710
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.245
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.147 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:17.116
I think it's safe to say
at this point

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:18.618
that the president
of the United States

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.086
is undermining public health.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.421
And I'm not just saying that

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.356
because he looks like
an "Outbreak" monkey

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.225
that escaped from a lab.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.592
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.195
Trump keeps lying to people
about the potential threat

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.230
posed by the spread
of the coronavirus

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.033
while the United States
lags behind other countries

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.202
in testing, even though
we've had time to learn

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.403
from their experiences.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:38.871
One infectious disease expert

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:41.374
called the lack
of widespread accurate testing

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.475
a national scandal.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:45.144
For example, the CDC website
said today

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.748
that 1,500 patients
had been tested just at CDC.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.383
Meanwhile,
"Bloomberg News" reported

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.918
that in a short space of time,

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:55.721
South Korea has managed to test
more than 140,000 people,

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:58.657
and they're using an ingenious
new way to do it.

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:02.362
-Outside of China, South Korea
has the most coronavirus cases.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:05.498
They've come up with
a new innovative way to test

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.499
for the virus in the form
of a drive-through.

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:09.102
-I'm going to show you

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.136
drive-through coronavirus
testing.

00:01:11.136 --> 00:01:14.407
This is a free service
that the city of Goyang

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.875
is offering anybody.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.878
Vehicles come through here,
and you get a questionnaire.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.113
You get your hands sanitized,

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:23.416
and then you go through
a number of stations here.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.851
The patients
never get out of the car.

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:27.920
They come in,
they fill out questionnaires,

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:31.090
find out whether or not
they're in a risk category,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.859
and while sitting in their cars,

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:36.262
the nurses will swab their
nostrils and their throats,

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.397
take samples,
and then the results

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:41.233
will come in within
two to three days.

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:44.670
This could be a model
for countries like the U.S.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.071
that are just starting to

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:49.409
deal with their first
coronavirus cases.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.277
-Of course, it should be
a model for us.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.280
Look, we might be bad at stuff
like health care, education,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.716
gun control, climate change,
housing, criminal justice,

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.985
and gender equality,
but nobody is better than us

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:01.988
at drive-throughs!
I mean, come on!

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.722
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:03.722 --> 00:02:08.728
And nothing, nothing should
appeal to our president more

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.630
than treating healthcare
like fast food.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.199
All we have to do is put
"coronavirus testing"

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.701
on the menu at every Wendy's,
and he'd go get one himself.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.804
[ As Trump ] Yeah, I'll have
four bacon cheeseburgers,

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:22.475
two Frosties, chicken nuggets,
and a cheek swab. Yeah.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:25.511
And maybe supersize that swab.
I've got cheeks like a mainsail.

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:26.679
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.047
[ Normal voice ] And yet,
we haven't gotten truth,

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:30.049
transparency, or testing
from the president.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.551
And that's because
from the very moment

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.353
news of the outbreak
began to spread,

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.954
Trump seemed to want
to wish it away

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.789
by denying the reality
of the situation

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.957
and telling people that one day,

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.893
the virus would just
magically disappear.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.462
-You have 15 people,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.263
and the 15 within
a couple of days

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.331
is going to be down
to close to zero.

00:02:46.331 --> 00:02:47.767
We're going down, not up.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.736
We're going very substantially
down, not up.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.270
I really think, doctor,
you ought to treat this

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.905
like you treat the flu, right?

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:55.841
And, you know, it's going
to be -- it's going to be --

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:57.710
Looks like by April, you know,
in theory,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.813
when it gets a little warmer,
it miraculously goes away.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:01.647
Hope that's true.

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:03.116
It's going to disappear.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.551
One day, it's like a miracle,
it will disappear.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:08.521
-As a general rule, never trust
someone's medical advice

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.955
when they use the word
"miracle."

00:03:09.955 --> 00:03:12.991
If you ask someone to look
at a rash, and they say,

00:03:12.991 --> 00:03:14.693
"It will go away,"
and you ask how,

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:16.062
and they say, "Like a miracle,"

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.631
you need to go buy
some ointment.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.633
Also, I don't trust Donald Trump
on the subject

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.801
of medical advice or miracles.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:25.138
-I have a great relationship
with God.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.639
God is the ultimate.
I mean, God created this.

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:31.010
So, uh, nobody,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.978
no thing, no --
there's nothing like God.

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:35.481
The Bible certainly is one of --
if not --

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.083
I mean, it is the book.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.718
-Do you actively go to church?

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.953
-Well, I go as much as I can,

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:43.922
always on Christmas,
always on Easter,

00:03:43.922 --> 00:03:48.027
and during the Sundays,
I'm a Sunday church person.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:51.864
-Oh, are you
a Sunday church person?

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:55.901
As opposed to, like, a Tuesday
afternoon church person?

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:59.305
Trump sounds like an atheist cop
going undercover as a priest

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.607
to spy on a bunch
of Catholic mobsters.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:07.213
"So, uh, Father,
what do you think

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.147
of our Lord and savior,
Jesus Christ?"

00:04:09.147 --> 00:04:10.282
[ As Trump ] Oh, J.C.?

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:11.751
Well, you know,
he's just the ultimate.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:15.087
And the Bible, of course,
that's just the book, you know?

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:18.357
And I go to church on Sundays.
You guys, too?

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:20.493
Get me out of here!
They're on to me!

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.661
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.228
[ Normal voice ]
Trump's been trying to pretend

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:24.630
the problem doesn't exist

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.966
because he knows
he'll get blamed for it.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:30.203
And he knows that because if
he weren't president right now,

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:33.205
he'd definitely be blaming
whoever was president.

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:36.976
In fact, yesterday, he even lied
and blamed a past president

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.845
for the current lack of testing.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:42.148
-The Obama administration
made a decision on testing

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:45.684
that turned out to be very
detrimental to what we're doing

00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:49.221
and we undid that decision
a few days ago

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:51.190
so that the testing
can take place

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.826
in a much more accurate
and rapid fashion.

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:56.962
-You can't blame Obama
for something that didn't exist

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:58.831
when he left office.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:01.100
[ As Trump ] Obama should
have never green-lit "Cats."

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:06.405
I mean, you either go full cats
or full people.

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:07.674
[ Normal voice ] And it won't
surprise you to learn

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:09.208
that this lie
was immediately debunked.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.677
Even the White House
couldn't explain it.

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:14.179
CNN reported that a source close
to the coronavirus task force

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:17.049
said it's not clear where Trump
got his information.

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:18.951
I have an idea
where he got it --

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.486
the same place he gets
all his ideas.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:24.523
I won't say where it is, but I
just hope he washed his hands.

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:27.226
Trump knows this whole thing
could be a challenge for him

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.894
politically and for the economy,

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:29.862
which is all that matters
to him.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.096
In fact, MSNBC reported

00:05:31.096 --> 00:05:33.499
that during Trump's trip
to India last month,

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.902
he was paying close attention
to TV news reports,

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:38.270
not about the virus,
but about the stock market.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.506
-Our reporting indicates
that while he was in India

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:43.142
he was watching the stock market
reaction very closely.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.744
He was very nervous and upset

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:47.680
to see what was happening
with the stock market.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.149
He seemed to be more aware
of what was happening

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.551
with the stock market than
what was actually happening

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.620
with developments
with the virus.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.255
-Of course,
because the stock market

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.823
is the only thing Trump
cares about.

00:05:57.823 --> 00:06:00.426
If you told Trump
that spreading the coronavirus

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.994
would actually help
the stock market,

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.462
he'd be doing press conferences

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:05.498
giving people the opposite
advice of doctors.

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.599
[ As Trump ] Remember
not to block your sneezes,

00:06:07.599 --> 00:06:08.867
lick stuff in public,

00:06:08.867 --> 00:06:10.837
and just touch your face
as much as possible.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:14.740
Just really get your fingers
in there, knead it like dough.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.609
[ Normal voice ]
Trump desperately wants to wish

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.978
the situation away to avoid
political accountability.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.779
That's why he decided
to call in

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:23.215
to his favorite propaganda
network, Fox News,

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:26.486
and spread disinformation
about the virus last night.

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.321
For example,
the World Health Organization

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:30.889
announced this week that
the official mortality rate

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:33.859
for the coronavirus so far
has been 3.4%

00:06:33.859 --> 00:06:36.295
compared to the flu
which is about 0.1%.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.297
Now, with aggressive measures
in testing,

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:39.465
experts say
it's certainly possible

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.600
that number will come down.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.801
Instead,
Trump told Fox News host,

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:44.370
Sean Hannity,
in a phone interview

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.439
that he straight-up
doesn't believe those numbers.

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:49.808
-We had a report today
that global death rate at 3.4%,

00:06:49.808 --> 00:06:53.745
and a report that the Olympics
could be delayed.

00:06:53.745 --> 00:06:55.581
Your reaction to that?

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:59.152
-Well, I think the 3.4%
is really a false number.

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:01.620
Now, this is just my hunch.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.488
I think that
that number is very high.

00:07:03.488 --> 00:07:05.491
I think the number --
personally, I would say

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.559
the number is way under 1%.

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:09.562
-Why are you going
on national television

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:11.697
and contradicting experts
based on a hunch?

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:14.533
First of all, the only hunch
of yours that I trust

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:17.369
is the one in your back after
an hour at one of your rallies.

00:07:17.369 --> 00:07:18.737
I mean, look at him.

00:07:18.737 --> 00:07:20.573
Normally, you only hide
your face like that

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.508
when you're at a restaurant
with your girlfriend

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:25.344
and you see your wife
at the other table.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:27.146
[ As Trump ] I love you, baby,
and I don't care who knows.

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:29.448
Oh [bleep] Carol!

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:31.183
[ Normal voice ]
So, Trump lied to viewers

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:32.351
about the mortality rate.

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:33.886
Then there's the fact
that employers

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.654
and public health experts
are urging anyone

00:07:35.654 --> 00:07:37.923
with any symptoms to stay home
and self-quarantine

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:40.459
rather than go to work and
potentially spread the virus.

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:42.961
Just yesterday,
a county in Washington

00:07:42.961 --> 00:07:44.597
officially recommended
teleworking,

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:45.864
and both Amazon and Facebook

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:47.733
asked their Seattle employees
to stay home.

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:49.935
But again, Dr. Trump disagreed.

00:07:49.935 --> 00:07:52.772
-A lot of people will have this,
and it's very mild.

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.740
They'll get better very rapidly.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.543
They don't even see a doctor.
They don't even call a doctor.

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:59.511
You never hear about
those people.

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:02.381
So, if, you know,
we have thousands

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:07.186
or hundreds of thousands of
people that get better just by,

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:10.155
you know, sitting around
and even going to work,

00:08:10.155 --> 00:08:12.792
some of them go to work,
but they get better.

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:13.993
-So now he's telling people

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:15.695
it's okay to go to work
if they're sick.

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:18.531
This from a guy who doesn't even
go to work when he's healthy.

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:19.699
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:21.734
So, the president
is spreading misinformation

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.068
about a public health crisis

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:24.970
in order to avoid
political consequences.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:28.173
But at least he knows
the name of the virus, right?

00:08:28.173 --> 00:08:31.844
-So, you can't put them down
in the category

00:08:31.844 --> 00:08:36.515
of the overall population
in terms of this corona flu.

00:08:36.515 --> 00:08:39.418
-Jesus. The corona flu?

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:43.122
Not only is he lying,
he's making up new diseases now.

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:45.992
[ As Trump ] It's called
the "corona swine Ebola flu."

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:47.392
We just came up with it.
It was very exciting.

00:08:47.392 --> 00:08:50.730
You can find it on the
drive-through menu at Wendy's.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.764
[ Normal voice ] This is
the kind of public health crisis

00:08:52.764 --> 00:08:53.999
that tests the competence

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:55.801
and honesty of our president,
and obviously,

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:58.003
Trump is completely unequipped
on both counts.

00:08:58.003 --> 00:09:00.406
We need truth, transparency,
and testing,

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:02.341
and we're not going to get it
from Donald Trump.

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:04.976
Then again, that's...
-Just my hunch.

00:09:04.976 --> 00:09:06.579
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:06.579 --> 00:09:07.913
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:10.182 line:0%
